#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tether -- keep a coding agent's credentials, egress and spend outside the
machine it runs on.

Grown from leash for the microsandbox + nono PoC (design/tether-poc.md), in
the spirit of imp (https://github.com/metcalfc/imp): the agent is handed a
per-session capability string, never a credential. One gateway process, which the agent
cannot reach into, does four things:

  * injects real credentials into model-provider and git traffic
    (/anthropic/..., /openai/..., /github/...), so no key sits on the box
  * is the agent's only way out (HTTPS_PROXY + a network with no other
    route), and only lets it CONNECT to hosts on an allowlist
  * meters every model call per session from the response's own usage
    numbers, and refuses the next call once a daily cap is passed
  * writes one JSON line per decision, allow or deny, for `tether report`

    agent VM / container                gateway (outside)
    -----------------------------------------------------------
    claude  --ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL-->  /anthropic  + real key --> api.anthropic.com
    git     --insteadOf--------->    /github     + real token-> github.com
    npm/pip --HTTPS_PROXY------->    CONNECT allowlist -------> registry.npmjs.org
    curl evil.example ---------->    403, audited

Stdlib only. Python 3.10+.

    tether init   -c policy.json   mint session capabilities, write run/tether/<session>.env
    tether serve  -c policy.json   run the gateway
    tether report -c policy.json   spend and denials per session, from the audit log
"""

